{
  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3741",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits, including Kcna3, Kcnd1, and Kcna6, which are all involved in outward or delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. These channels are critical for maintaining electrical activity in cardiac and neuromuscular systems. The evidence suggests that Dalfampridine may modulate these channels through binding, potentially influencing their function and activity. The shared involvement of Kcna5 in the activity of these channels implies a possible functional link between Dalfampridine and Kcna5, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of potassium channels in cellular electrophysiology and suggests that Dalfampridine could exert its effects through a mechanism involving these channels.",
